page('06  /  DEMONSTRATION','From booking to payment')
p('Run the following calls one at a time in a disposable demo database. Confirm user 1 and charger 2 exist. Choose a free interval, and continue only when the preceding call returns SUCCESS. The example records a simulated payment; it does not move money.')
code("CALL sp_book_charger_slot(1, 2,\n '2026-11-21 10:00:00', '2026-11-21 11:00:00',\n @booking, @status, @message);\nSELECT @booking, @status, @message;\n\nCALL sp_start_charging_session(@booking,\n @session, @status, @message);\nSELECT @session, @status, @message;\n\nCALL sp_complete_charging_session(@session, 10.000,\n @amount, @status, @message);\nSELECT @amount, @status, @message;\n\nCALL sp_process_payment(@session, 'UPI', 'COMPLETED',\n @status, @message);\nSELECT @status, @message;\n\nSELECT * FROM vw_payment_audit_log\nWHERE session_id = @session;")
h('What the operator should observe')
p('Booking creates a confirmed reservation. Session start captures the charger tariff and records the current timestamp. Completion records the supplied energy, changes session status and creates a pending invoice. Payment processing updates the invoice status and timestamp. These are expected source behaviors, not newly executed results.')
h('Practice basic CRUD')
code("START TRANSACTION;\nINSERT INTO users(full_name,email,phone)\nVALUES ('Demo User','report.demo@example.in','9000000000');\nSET @demo = LAST_INSERT_ID();\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE user_id = @demo;\nUPDATE users SET phone='9000000001' WHERE user_id=@demo;\nDELETE FROM users WHERE user_id=@demo;\nROLLBACK;")
p('Run the practice transaction in one connection. The workflow procedures manage their own transactions and should not be nested inside this example transaction.')
page('07  /  SQL IN PRACTICE','Queries that explain the design')
h('Find operational fast chargers')
code("SELECT charger_code, power_kw, rate_per_kwh\nFROM chargers\nWHERE charger_type='DC' AND power_kw >= 60\n  AND status='ACTIVE'\nORDER BY power_kw DESC;")
p('Filtering selects eligible hardware; ordering places the highest power first. Reservation availability requires a separate time overlap check.')
h('Join drivers to their reservations')
code('SELECT b.booking_id, u.full_name, c.charger_code,\n       s.station_name, b.start_time, b.status\nFROM bookings b\nJOIN users u ON b.user_id=u.user_id\nJOIN chargers c ON b.charger_id=c.charger_id\nJOIN stations s ON c.station_id=s.station_id;')
p('Foreign keys reconstruct the customer, hardware and location context without copying those attributes into bookings.')
h('Summarize energy by charger type')
code("SELECT c.charger_type, COUNT(*) AS sessions,\n       SUM(cs.energy_kwh) AS total_kwh,\n       AVG(cs.energy_kwh) AS average_kwh\nFROM charging_sessions cs\nJOIN bookings b ON cs.booking_id=b.booking_id\nJOIN chargers c ON b.charger_id=c.charger_id\nWHERE cs.status='COMPLETED'\nGROUP BY c.charger_type\nHAVING SUM(cs.energy_kwh)>50;")
p('WHERE filters records before grouping; HAVING filters the resulting groups. The original demonstration script also includes MIN, MAX, subqueries, CTEs, DENSE_RANK, LAG and EXPLAIN.')
h('Full SQL companion')
p('Complete_SQL_Companion.md contains every supplied SQL file and all 32 original demonstration queries. Original executable scripts remain in their project folders. The companion is a reference collection, not a single script to execute from top to bottom.')
page('08  /  IMPLEMENTATION','Procedures triggers and views')
table(['Stored procedure','Responsibility'],[['sp_book_charger_slot','Validate user, lock charger and check overlap'],['sp_start_charging_session','Check booking and capture tariff'],['sp_complete_charging_session','Record energy and create invoice'],['sp_calculate_bill','Return joined bill details'],['sp_process_payment','Update payment state and timestamp'],['sp_station_revenue_report','Aggregate station activity and revenue']])
h('Four targeted triggers')
p('The booking insert trigger validates time order. The session insert trigger supplies a tariff when missing or nonpositive. The session update trigger synchronizes booking completion. The payment update trigger supplies a settlement timestamp when transitioning to completed. There is no trigger that prevents overlapping bookings or makes historical prices immutable.')
h('Five reporting views')
table(['View','Use'],[['vw_active_chargers','Operational charger catalog'],['vw_user_booking_history','User reservations with station details'],['vw_charging_session_details','Energy, duration and calculated bill'],['vw_payment_audit_log','Invoice and payment context'],['vw_station_revenue_summary','Station activity and revenue summary']])
h('Transactions and indexes')
p('Workflow procedures use transactions, error handlers and rollback. Booking locks the charger row with SELECT FOR UPDATE. The source includes indexes for station geography, charger status/type, reservation overlap, user history, session dates and payment status/method. An index is not evidence of a measured response time.')
p('Two connection concurrency tests remain necessary. The procedure’s earlier ordinary lookup may establish a repeatable read snapshot before a competing transaction commits. Direct SQL also bypasses several business checks. These boundaries matter when explaining the implementation in a viva.')
page('09  /  EVALUATION','Results and conclusion')
h('Evidence and results')
p('The seed source contains 20 users, 8 stations, 24 chargers, 60 bookings, 30 sessions and 25 payments. Static recomputation gives 20 completed payments totaling INR 19,779.73. Session 1 records 42.500 kWh at INR 19.50 per kWh, producing INR 828.75. These are source based calculations, not fresh live database results.')
table(['Finding','Implication'],[['Saved total differs from seed total','Saved monthly output of INR 18,942.28 needs reconciliation'],['Bookings 28–30 completed; sessions in progress','Cross table lifecycle validation is incomplete'],['Operational charger SUM follows booking join','The summary view may count one charger repeatedly'],['Saved test summary claims 20 PASS results','No fresh run; TC 19 and TC 20 have weak assertions']])
h('Testing coverage')
p('The supplied harness covers user insertion, duplicate email, foreign keys, invalid power and times, charger status, booking overlap, duplicate sessions, negative energy, billing, rate capture, payment and cleanup. Current execution status is NOT EXECUTED for this report. Historical PASS claims do not establish concurrent safety or complete reconciliation. The harness creates an auxiliary log table and performs cleanup, so use a disposable copy.')
h('Conclusion and future scope')
p('The project demonstrates relational modeling, a justified 3NF design, reusable SQL reporting and a charging workflow implemented through procedures. Its next priorities are stronger lifecycle checks, corrected summary counting, reconciled sample records and concurrent tests. A user interface, hardware integration, maps, notifications and real payment processing are future extensions.')
